Now I unpack.
I open my first box.
I put the books on the shelf.
I put the clothes in the wardrobe.
I look down into the next box.
There lies a photo under a book.
It is a photo of my family.
My mother, my father, my sister and my brother.
Even my dog, Lola, is in the picture.
They are all in Mexico.
I pick the photo up and smile.
I walk over to the table.
I put the photo on the table.
Now the photo stands on the table by the lamp.
I look at my family.
"Now you are here too," I say softly.
